Phase 2 item 3 — Stop/Pause/Steer reach the in-flight run
==========================================================
Node: M2.7 (Basic Prompt Compiler and one-agent runtime)
Defect: Future-tasks.md section 2 item 5 (audit 2026-09-06)
Revision: commit (amended on phase2/loop-hardening; implementation commit
includes this file) — base commit before amend: "Phase 2.3: Stop/Pause/
Steer reach the in-flight run"
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC timestamps

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: BROKEN-DRIFTED — events only)
----------------------------------------------------------------
StopTask/PauseTask/SteerTask wrote durable events; nothing reached the
in-flight model stream or the execd broker run (Stop during a 30s tool
waited it out); steer notes were stored and never injected.

- one_agent: RunControl trait — steer notes drain into the conversation
  as user messages BEFORE the next invoke; StopTask aborts and PauseTask
  parks at the turn boundary (cancelled/paused result flags, run-level
  failure codes "cancelled"/"paused").
- scheduler: RunControls registry of live RunSignals; run_task registers
  around the run; surface dispatch signals stop/pause FIRST, then writes
  the durable lifecycle event; steer rides a race-free per-task outbox
  (a note queued before the run registers still lands on the next
  boundary — found by the E2E timing race, fixed before commit).
- LiveGatewayTransport: tokio::select! races the provider stream against
  the run's cancel flag (100ms cadence).
- terminal: run_capture_cancellable — the wait polls the flag, kills the
  broker run (no orphan process) and returns typed Cancelled.
- Post-run: cancelled/paused runs never overwrite the durable task state
  with a run outcome or a provider park (the TaskWaiting park is skipped
  when the cancel flag fired).
- proto lifecycle RPC comments updated to the real semantics; TS bindings
  regenerated in the same commit.

